# --- CI follow-up: the impact scan blocked, and the RULE was the problem -----

# `scan` failed with:
#   blocker · conversation-flow-change-needs-test · services/gateway/src/routes/orb-livekit.ts
#   "changes conversation-flow code but adds/updates no conversation-flow test"
#
# I HAD added tests. Checked the rule's own regex rather than assuming:
node -e "const RE=/^services\/gateway\/test\/.*(conversation|...|tool).*\.(test|spec)\.(ts|tsx)$/i; ..."
#   -> false  services/gateway/test/routes/orb-livekit.test.ts
#   -> false  services/gateway/test/orb/live/upstream/cascade-health-payload.test.ts
#
# The rule lists routes/orb-live.ts and routes/orb-livekit.ts as flow SOURCE but
# its FLOW_TEST_RE matched none of the keywords in those routes' OWN canonical
# test files. So it flagged a source file and then refused to accept a real test
# of that same file, in the place it is already tested.
#
# Two dishonest ways out were available and both rejected:
#   - rename a test file until it hits a keyword
#   - claim `flow-test-exempt` (documented for "comment / log / rename") for a
#     change that alters an HTTP response body — not behaviour-free
# Both launder a guess into a green check (VTID-03696's own conclusion).

# Fix: added `orb-live` to FLOW_TEST_RE (covers orb-livekit by substring).
# Confirmed the gate did NOT become a rubber stamp:
#   accepts test/routes/orb-livekit.test.ts        -> true
#   accepts test/routes/orb-live.test.ts           -> true
#   accepts test/orb/conversation-flow.contract    -> true   (unchanged)
#   rejects test/routes/wallet.test.ts             -> false  (still discriminates)
#   rejects services/gateway/src/routes/orb-livekit.ts -> false

# Verified editing an EXISTING rule does not trip new-impact-rule-needs-seed-migration
# (that fires on status === 'A').

# 4 supertest cases added to test/routes/orb-livekit.test.ts hitting the REAL
# route, incl. the enabled-but-not-effective state and a leak check.  -> 89/89

# 6 tests pinning the rule's satisfiability, reading FLOW_TEST_RE out of the
# rule source so they cannot drift from what CI runs. Mutation-verified:
#   removing `|orb-live` -> 3 failed / 3 passed; restored -> 6/6

npx tsc --noEmit                                          # clean
npx jest test/orb/ test/routes/orb-livekit.test.ts test/scripts/
#   -> 1906 passing, 6 pre-existing todo
